# Seabright Culverts (biome: culverts) - 50x50, four quarters on a canal cross
# Symbols: . floor  + start  W canal water (impassable)
#   walls, ONE STONE PER QUARTER so you always know where you are:
#   % old brick (NW)   = slate (NE)   # mossgrown (SW)   B masonry (SE)
#   P = fern patch (walkable)   F = glow-flies (walkable)
# Monsters: r rat  v bat  t thief bug  y Golden Thief Bug (boss)
#
# THE CANALS cross at mid-map (x24-25 and y24-25), walkways on both banks,
# and exactly FOUR plank bridges out along the arms: x11-12 and x37-38 over
# the east-west channel, y11-12 and y37-38 over the north-south one. At the
# crossing lies THE CONFLUENCE: Sewerman Garran stands on its north-west
# plaza, the last valve (7) on its south-east one.
#
# NW - THE OLD WORKS (% brick): the entrance sewer, the tool room, and two
#   round cisterns: R1 (x3-9, y7-13, valve 1 at its heart) and the great
#   cistern R3 (x12-20, y12-19, valve 2 + a chest). Doors to the walkways at
#   (21,5)... via the tool room east wall, (5,21) and (16,21).
# NE - THE SLUICEWORKS (= slate): five long galleries linked at ALTERNATING
#   ends (east, west, east, west...) - a switchback, not a maze. Valve 3 at
#   gallery 1's east end, valve 4 at gallery 4's west mouth; the iron chest
#   pays out the full switchback at gallery 5's east dead end. Bats roost.
# SW - THE OVERGROWN (# mossy): grotto country - ferns, glow-flies, and the
#   THIEF-BUG NEST (x11-19); the mud gallery (y37-38) links to the deep
#   grotto (valve 5) and the bugs' larder. THE POCKET: a one-wide slit at
#   (3,46) hides an iron chest - suspicious dead end, worth the squeeze.
# SE - THE VAULT WARREN (B masonry): a grid of storerooms (barrels, vermin),
#   valve 6 in the east hall, and in the far corner THE TREASURE VAULT:
#   the Golden Thief Bug over the golden chest, door at (42,45).
# Monsters (unchanged counts): r x19, v x25, t x28, y x1. Valves: 7.
